  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/env-c/209",
  "definition": "Relevance of Prior Violations",
  "effectiveDate": "2007-03-25",
  "historyNote": "#6960, eff 3-25-99; ss by #7562, eff 9-26-01; ss by #8851-A, eff 3-25-07",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-C 209.04",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-c200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-C 209.04 Relevance of Prior Violations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-C 209.04 Relevance of Prior Violations.\n\n(a) The department shall not base a decision to suspend, revoke, or refuse to renew a license or to deny a license application on prior violation(s) not documented by one or more enforcement actions that arose in a program other than the program to which the license application or license pertains unless the prior violations(s) can reasonably be found to be relevant to the license or application under consideration.\n\n(b) Any prior violation(s) arising in the same program as the license or application under consideration shall be deemed to be relevant to the pending license action.\n\nSource. #6960, eff 3-25-99; ss by #7562, eff 9-26-01; ss by #8851-A, eff 3-25-07",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-c200.html"
